{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0D15", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$DQ_X(\\mathcal{F}) \\to DQ_X(\\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-perfect-section-better-coherator}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-thickening-space-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d842b790843a74c90bd00be3a28bc9cb71962cdce8313ed2c9df1b16d2a72475", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6180dc4082003906a19a4caf0e5cf9ff80e4a0b2323ea28277db6a2666a97f5", "source_text": "In the situation above assume that <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated\nand that <MATH_0002>\n(Derived Categories of Spaces, Section\n<REF_0001>)\nis an isomorphism. Then the functor <MATH_0003> is an equivalence of categories.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e2c5d2af2180358d52e3f845284711e213cb6cfef0d938af799e771af1ff7483", "unit_id": "tag:0D3P:statement"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0D15", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\NL_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$D_\\QCoh(\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{F}) \\longrightarrow\n\\Ext^i_X(\\NL_{X/B}, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\oplus \\mathcal{G}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-netherlander-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-huge-diagram-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-choices-ringed-topoi}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4ee1cdf5311eff108e2e1b009e81c9f982f40ab5aedd9834828a244ca217698b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a5d272bf80d62bd07c44378a956829f07d714e68584cbce7386cd5d7d80051e", "source_text": "Recall that <MATH_0001> is an object of <MATH_0002>, see\nMore on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nHence our assumption implies the maps\n<MATH_0003>\nare isomorphisms for all <MATH_0004>. This implies our functor is fully\nfaithful by Lemma <REF_0002>.\nOn the other hand, the functor is essentially surjective by\nLemma <REF_0003> because\nwe have the solutions <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> in both categories.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4bba49b5b4c2bbe1360c8c0190c7113be8ff588f48f9570c9aab4cf6c6f21fde", "unit_id": "tag:0D3P:proof"}
